  "insights": [
   "The AI trade is facing a unit-economics crisis where token prices are collapsing faster than consumption is growing, undermining the revenue assumptions used to underwrite massive hyperscaler CapEx.",
   "Silicon Data\u2019s LLM Token Expenditure Index fell 29% in August to a record low of $0.97 per million tokens, down over 50% from the May peak.",
   "OpenRouter token volume rose 47% MoM in August, but dollar spend increased only 7%, indicating a significant mix shift toward cheaper open-weight models and aggressive price competition.",
   "Hyperscaler CapEx is projected at $737 billion for 2026, roughly 38% of revenue, creating a massive debt burden that is now being repriced by credit markets.",
   "78 of 91 hyperscaler bonds issued in 2026 were trading cheaper than their issuance price by late August, signaling that credit markets are pricing in ROIC compression before equity markets.",
   "The shift toward local inference and on-device processing (e.g., RTX Spark-class laptops, Mac Studios) is turning former API customers into one-time hardware buyers, threatening the 40% software annuity model.",
   "Broadcom remains a high-conviction Buy for Goldman, with management guiding AI semi revenue to double to $115bn in FY27 and again to $230bn in FY28, citing Anthropic as a major customer.",
   "The market is transitioning from a capability-driven bull market to a price-taker regime where infinite demand does not guarantee profitability if the price per token cannot service the underlying debt.",
